  "verdict": "After holding Refsdal out and treating each observed-delay uncertainty as a shared system-level error, Encore plus H0pe-AB give kappa_lens = -0.442 +/- 0.282.  This predicts a Refsdal residual of +116.8 +/- 74.5 d, compared with the covariance-corrected +29.6 +/- 10.2 d; the difference is 1.16 sigma.  The external prediction is therefore statistically consistent but too imprecise to close the amplitude test, and its central value is larger than Refsdal by a factor 3.9.  A generic fractional-delay model remains modestly preferred over the log-magnification proxy (Delta AIC = 1.23)."
